From 3696656596b8252c01080bbd78b79d32641df4c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 01:35:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] World pause and Play Mode click-to-inspect

* LogicThread.set_world_paused(owner, paused) / world_paused: per-owner pause
  requests. While any is held a play tick advances nothing in the world
  (player, movers, doors, I/O timers, light fades, triggers, props, physics,
  projectiles, portals) but plugins still tick with the use key, so a game's
  menus keep working; look and fire input is drained, not queued. The
  MonsterAIThread idles and drops the paused time instead of catching up.
  Entering or leaving Play Mode drops every request.
* engine/actor_pick.py: which actor a screen ray hits, from the published
  EntityTable (monster rows, not hidden, sphere = billboard) and RenderTable
  (visible solid brushes occlude; triggers, glass, fog, water, glow and
  subtract brushes do not). Vectorised; no walk over scene objects.
* QtGameView.begin_actor_pick(on_pick=None): pauses the world, frees the
  cursor, shows a banner naming the actor under the cursor, and on a left
  click hands the actor over (default: the Entity Inspector). Esc or a right
  click cancels. The ray leaves the camera the frame was drawn from, so it
  is right in first person and overhead. MainWindow.begin_actor_pick
  delegates, for plugin commands.

Tests: tests/engine/test_world_pause.py (owners, paused tick vs unpaused
control, AI thread idle/no catch-up) and tests/engine/test_actor_pick.py
(real EntityTable/RenderTable picks and the view's pick mode). Full suite:
4006 passed, 5 skipped.

